y been underdiagnosed and undertreated</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborative Provider Network:</strong> Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inclusive Culture:</strong> Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com/\"><strong><u>Allara</u></strong></a>, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Allara https://www.allarahealth.com is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved health outcomes https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.\n\n\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe’re hiring Registered Dietitians who want to focus on what matters most: delivering exceptional care to women who have historically been underserved. To learn more about our mission and clinical approach, visit allarahealth.com http://allarahealth.com.\n\n\n\nLocation: Fully remote within the U.S.\n\n\n\nYour Impact\n\n - Analyze intake assessments, including medical history, dietary habits, laboratory results, and more.\n\n - Conduct diet and lifestyle counseling and education sessions via video, including offering general movement, sleep, or stress management advice as needed and related to nutrition care.\n\n - Employ Allara’s provided nutrition training and educational materials to ensure consistent care while adapting to patient needs.\n\n - Incorporate motivational interviewing and behavior change techniques throughout the continuity of care.\n\n - Collaborate with APRNs and MDs involved in the medical management of your patients.\n\n - Maintain accurate and up-to-date patient records.\n\n - Dedicate a minimum of 10 patient-facing hours per week in addition to administrative time.\n\n - Responsibilities also include charting, addressing patient inquiries, and responding to administrative tasks and messages in a timely manner.\n\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n - Certification: Registered Dietitian with current certification from the Commission on Dietetic Registration (CDR).\n\n - Experience: 1 year of experience treating patients with complex women’s health conditions (strongly desired).\n\n - Clinical Independence: Proven ability to function as an autonomous provider with strong diagnostic judgment and critical thinking skills\n\n - Communication: Exceptional written and verbal communication, with an emphasis on compassion and clarity\n\n - Webside Manner: A natural ability to build trust and connection with patients in a virtual setting\n\n - Evidence-Based Practice: A genuine commitment to delivering care rooted in current clinical research\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Comfortable working across multiple platforms, including EMR systems, text expanders, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling tools\n\n - Telemedicine Experience: Prior telehealth experience is a plus\n\n - State License Requirements & Hiring Considerations: An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered state license to practice as a Registered Dietitian in at least one U.S. state is required.\n\n\n\nA note on state licensing: All active and pending licenses held at the time of application are collected and reviewed during our process. Hiring decisions reflect current state-level needs, which evolve over time. Applicants may not move forward immediately if there is no active need in their licensed states. We regularly revisit candidates as needs expand and when experience, licensure, and role requirements align.\n\n\n\nWhat Allara Offers\n\n - 1099 Contract: The flexibility and autonomy of an independent contractor arrangement\n\n - Competitive Compensation: Per-visit rates plus additional pay for charting, administrative tasks, and other patient-related work\n\n - 1099 Longevity Recognition Bonus\n\n - Continuing Education: Access to multiple free, live CEU sessions every month, plus a Women's Health Certificate of Training launching in 2027!\n\n - Fully Remote: Work from anywhere in the U.S.\n\n - Malpractice Insurance: Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you\n\n - Mission-Driven Work: Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated\n\n - Collaborative Provider Network: Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians\n\n - Inclusive Culture: Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging\n\n\n\n\n\nAt Allara https://www.allarahealth.com/, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"549073b4-7333-4b9d-8ff6-6cccf0d3e67a","title":"Remote Psychiatrist - Part-Time 1099","department":"Clinical","team":"Psychiatry - Physician","employmentType":"Contract","location":"California","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T18:53:49.051+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/549073b4-7333-4b9d-8ff6-6cccf0d3e67a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/549073b4-7333-4b9d-8ff6-6cccf0d3e67a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com\"><strong>Allara</strong></a> is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf\"><strong>health outcomes</strong></a>. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're seeking a <strong>Consulting Psychiatrist </strong>to launch Allara's Psychiatry Service Line, as Allara Health expands its care model to include psychiatric services for women navigating the intersection of hormonal and mental health, and we're looking for a board-certified psychiatrist to support the launch right from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a consulting engagement supporting the clinical infrastructure for Allara's psychiatry service line. You'll work closely with our clinical and operations leadership to design the protocols, safeguards, and hiring standards that will define how we deliver psychiatric care to our patients. Once launched, you’ll treat your own panel of patients as well as provide supervision and case consultations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Fully remote within the U.S.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your Impact </strong><br /><br /><strong>Pre-Launch</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop clinical protocols for the treatment of mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD, including medication management and therapeutic modalities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design safety and escalation protocols for behavioral health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a hiring rubric and assessment framework for PMHNP candidates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in initial PMHNP interviews alongside our clinical team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Post-Launch</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate 50% of your time to treating patients experiencing mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supervise PMHNPs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide case consultations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support on ad-hoc escalations</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Board Certification: </strong>Active board certification in Psychiatry through the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN) or the American Osteopathic Board of Neurology and Psychiatry (AOBNP).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Licensure:</strong> An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered medical license in at least one of the following states: California, Florida, New York, or Texas. An IMLC license can be considered if willing to obtain an IMLC state mentioned above. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience: </strong>Minimum of 5 years of post-residency clinical experience as a practicing psychiatrist, with a focus on outpatient care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Women's Mental Health: </strong>Demonstrated experience treating conditions at the intersection of hormonal and mental health, including depression, anxiety, and PMDD.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Supervision:</strong> Experience supervising or collaborating with psychiatric nurse practitioners (PMHNPs) or other advanced practice providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems Building: </strong>Ability to translate clinical rigor into scalable protocols, safety standards, and hiring frameworks in a fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication &amp; Webside Manner: </strong>Exceptional written and verbal communication, with a strong ability to connect with patients virtually and deliver empathetic, evidence-based care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency:</strong> Comfortable navigating multiple screens and tools such as EMR, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling platforms.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in a telehealth or high-growth care delivery environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing behavioral health safety and escalation protocols.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Commitment</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pre-Launch: </strong>5 hours/wk from September-26 to February-27</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Post- Launch:</strong> 10 hours/wk from March-27 onwards</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Allara Offers</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1099 Contract: </strong>The flexibility and autonomy of an independent contractor arrangement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation:</strong> $200/hr.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1099 Longevity Recognition Bonus</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote: </strong>Work from anywhere in the U.S.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Scheduling:</strong> Set hours that fit your life, not the other way around</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Malpractice Insurance: </strong>Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-Driven Work: </strong>Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborative Provider Network: </strong>Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inclusive Culture:</strong> Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com/\"><strong><u>Allara</u></strong></a>, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Allara https://www.allarahealth.com is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved health outcomes https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.\n\n\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe're seeking a Consulting Psychiatrist to launch Allara's Psychiatry Service Line, as Allara Health expands its care model to include psychiatric services for women navigating the intersection of hormonal and mental health, and we're looking for a board-certified psychiatrist to support the launch right from the ground up.\n\n\n\nThis is a consulting engagement supporting the clinical infrastructure for Allara's psychiatry service line. You'll work closely with our clinical and operations leadership to design the protocols, safeguards, and hiring standards that will define how we deliver psychiatric care to our patients. Once launched, you’ll treat your own panel of patients as well as provide supervision and case consultations.\n\n\n\nLocation: Fully remote within the U.S.\n\n\n\nYour Impact \n\nPre-Launch\n\n - Develop clinical protocols for the treatment of mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD, including medication management and therapeutic modalities\n\n - Design safety and escalation protocols for behavioral health\n\n - Build a hiring rubric and assessment framework for PMHNP candidates\n\n - Participate in initial PMHNP interviews alongside our clinical team\n\n\n\nPost-Launch\n\n - Allocate 50% of your time to treating patients experiencing mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD\n\n - Supervise PMHNPs\n\n - Provide case consultations\n\n - Support on ad-hoc escalations\n\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n - Board Certification: Active board certification in Psychiatry through the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN) or the American Osteopathic Board of Neurology and Psychiatry (AOBNP).\n\n - Licensure: An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered medical license in at least one of the following states: California, Florida, New York, or Texas. An IMLC license can be considered if willing to obtain an IMLC state mentioned above. \n\n - Experience: Minimum of 5 years of post-residency clinical experience as a practicing psychiatrist, with a focus on outpatient care.\n\n - Women's Mental Health: Demonstrated experience treating conditions at the intersection of hormonal and mental health, including depression, anxiety, and PMDD.\n\n - Supervision: Experience supervising or collaborating with psychiatric nurse practitioners (PMHNPs) or other advanced practice providers.\n\n - Systems Building: Ability to translate clinical rigor into scalable protocols, safety standards, and hiring frameworks in a fast-moving environment.\n\n - Communication & Webside Manner: Exceptional written and verbal communication, with a strong ability to connect with patients virtually and deliver empathetic, evidence-based care.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Comfortable navigating multiple screens and tools such as EMR, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling platforms.\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Prior experience in a telehealth or high-growth care delivery environment.\n\n - Experience designing behavioral health safety and escalation protocols.\n\n\n\nTime Commitment\n\n - Pre-Launch: 5 hours/wk from September-26 to February-27\n\n - Post- Launch: 10 hours/wk from March-27 onwards\n\n\n\nWhat Allara Offers\n\n - 1099 Contract: The flexibility and autonomy of an independent contractor arrangement\n\n - Compensation: $200/hr.\n\n - 1099 Longevity Recognition Bonus\n\n - Fully Remote: Work from anywhere in the U.S.\n\n - Flexible Scheduling: Set hours that fit your life, not the other way around\n\n - Malpractice Insurance: Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you\n\n - Mission-Driven Work: Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated\n\n - Collaborative Provider Network: Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians\n\n - Inclusive Culture: Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging\n\n\n\nAt Allara https://www.allarahealth.com/, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6450a180-cece-47e9-8341-764120ea48be","title":"Clinical Operations Associate","department":"Corporate","team":"Clinical Operations ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-24T19:30:10.517+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/6450a180-cece-47e9-8341-764120ea48be","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/6450a180-cece-47e9-8341-764120ea48be/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com\"><strong>Allara</strong></a> is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf\"><strong>health outcomes</strong></a>. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allara is building the leading telehealth platform for women's hormonal health, and our provider network is the engine that makes it run. With 500+ providers across 50 states and rapid growth ahead, getting every new provider trained, confident, and ready on their start date is critical to our success. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The<strong> Clinical Operations Associate</strong> is a curious self-starter who is agile in jumping in to solve the biggest problems across Clinical Operations, from keeping our provider pipeline moving to building care automations and more. You are the person who notices when something is about to slip <em>before</em> it slips, and who chases it down without needing to be asked twice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Hybrid (NYC). We value in-person collaboration and aim for at least three days per week in our NYC office, with flexibility as needed <strong>or</strong> fully remote within the U.S.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your Impact</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support the provider onboarding process</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track every incoming provider against their onboarding checklist, trainings, credentialing milestones, and start date, and keep that tracker accurate and current</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively follow up with providers who are falling behind on required trainings, and escalate when a delay puts a start date at risk</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor the onboarding pipeline for patterns: where are providers consistently getting stuck, and why</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep provider records (Airtable and related systems) clean, current, and trustworthy as a source of truth for the rest of the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work cross-functionally to identify and unblock bottlenecks</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Spot problems before they become problems</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flag at-risk start dates early, with enough lead time for the team to intervene</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Notice when a process, template, or handoff isn't working and raise it; you don't wait for something to break to mention it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring solutions, not just observations, when you flag an issue</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design clinical operations systems for automation and scale; this could include anything that touches provider journey, patient scheduling, clinical practice enablement, and more</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support the broader provider experience</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help maintain communications and templates (emails, reminders, checklists) so providers always know what's next and clarity is our default</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support ad hoc projects that improve the provider journey as the team continues to scale</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years of experience in operations, coordination, healthcare administration, or a similar execution-heavy role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized with strong attention to detail and ability to keep track of many moving parts with many competing and constantly shifting priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A true self-starter: you look for what's blocking progress rather than waiting to be told</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process-oriented but don’t get attached to a solution if you notice what you built is no longer working.  You iterate and move forward quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable asking questions and raising issues proactively - ready to offer a solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, professional written and verbal communicator - you balance setting expectations firmly but put forth a human-centric way of communicating</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data-literate: comfortable working in a tracker or database and keeping it accurate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible and adaptable: you iterate when needed as new issues arise – priorities shift, and you accept the challenge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI Curious: you’re excited about how evolving tools can continue to change and evolve your role</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in telehealth, healthcare operations, or a multi-stakeholder onboarding process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with tools like Airtable, Notion, Google Suite, Slack, Metabase, or similar operational platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to W2/1099 workforce classification nuances</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine interest in Allara's mission and improving the experience of the clinicians who deliver our care</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Allara Offers</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation &amp; Career Growth</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$70,0000 - $85,000 with opportunities for advancement <em><strong>**See note below</strong></em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development &amp; employee learning programs</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>**Note: </strong>This compensation range may be inclusive of several career levels at Allara and will be narrowed during the interview process based on the candidate’s experience and qualifications. Adjustments outside of this range may be considered for candidates whose qualifications significantly differ from those outlined in the job description.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Work Environment &amp; Flexibility</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-day hybrid in NYC</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unlimited PTO &amp; 11 company holidays</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical, dental, and vision benefits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health Savings Account (HSA) &amp; Flexible Spending Account (FSA)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Long- and short-term disability coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annual employee wellness stipend</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Family &amp; Future Planning</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Parental leave &amp; family planning support benefits</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Perks</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company-issued laptop</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annual work-from-home stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commuter benefits (if applicable)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A collaborative, mission-driven culture focused on improving patient care</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com/\"><strong><u>Allara</u></strong></a>, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Allara https://www.allarahealth.com is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved health outcomes https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.\n\n\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nAllara is building the leading telehealth platform for women's hormonal health, and our provider network is the engine that makes it run. With 500+ providers across 50 states and rapid growth ahead, getting every new provider trained, confident, and ready on their start date is critical to our success. \n\n\n\nThe Clinical Operations Associate is a curious self-starter who is agile in jumping in to solve the biggest problems across Clinical Operations, from keeping our provider pipeline moving to building care automations and more. You are the person who notices when something is about to slip before it slips, and who chases it down without needing to be asked twice.\n\n\n\nLocation: Hybrid (NYC). We value in-person collaboration and aim for at least three days per week in our NYC office, with flexibility as needed or fully remote within the U.S.\n\n\n\nYour Impact\n\nSupport the provider onboarding process\n\n - Track every incoming provider against their onboarding checklist, trainings, credentialing milestones, and start date, and keep that tracker accurate and current\n\n - Proactively follow up with providers who are falling behind on required trainings, and escalate when a delay puts a start date at risk\n\n - Monitor the onboarding pipeline for patterns: where are providers consistently getting stuck, and why\n\n - Keep provider records (Airtable and related systems) clean, current, and trustworthy as a source of truth for the rest of the team\n\n - Work cross-functionally to identify and unblock bottlenecks\n\n\n\nSpot problems before they become problems\n\n - Flag at-risk start dates early, with enough lead time for the team to intervene\n\n - Notice when a process, template, or handoff isn't working and raise it; you don't wait for something to break to mention it\n\n - Bring solutions, not just observations, when you flag an issue\n\n - Design clinical operations systems for automation and scale; this could include anything that touches provider journey, patient scheduling, clinical practice enablement, and more\n\n\n\nSupport the broader provider experience\n\n - Help maintain communications and templates (emails, reminders, checklists) so providers always know what's next and clarity is our default\n\n - Support ad hoc projects that improve the provider journey as the team continues to scale\n\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n - 3-5 years of experience in operations, coordination, healthcare administration, or a similar execution-heavy role\n\n - Highly organized with strong attention to detail and ability to keep track of many moving parts with many competing and constantly shifting priorities.\n\n - A true self-starter: you look for what's blocking progress rather than waiting to be told\n\n - Process-oriented but don’t get attached to a solution if you notice what you built is no longer working.  You iterate and move forward quickly.\n\n - Comfortable asking questions and raising issues proactively - ready to offer a solution.\n\n - Clear, professional written and verbal communicator - you balance setting expectations firmly but put forth a human-centric way of communicating\n\n - Data-literate: comfortable working in a tracker or database and keeping it accurate\n\n - Flexible and adaptable: you iterate when needed as new issues arise – priorities shift, and you accept the challenge\n\n - AI Curious: you’re excited about how evolving tools can continue to change and evolve your role\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience in telehealth, healthcare operations, or a multi-stakeholder onboarding process.\n\n - Familiarity with tools like Airtable, Notion, Google Suite, Slack, Metabase, or similar operational platforms.\n\n - Exposure to W2/1099 workforce classification nuances\n\n - Genuine interest in Allara's mission and improving the experience of the clinicians who deliver our care\n\n\n\nWhat Allara Offers\n\n - Compensation & Career Growth\n   \n   - $70,0000 - $85,000 with opportunities for advancement **See note below\n   \n   - Equity\n   \n   - Professional development & employee learning programs\n   \n   **Note: This compensation range may be inclusive of several career levels at Allara and will be narrowed during the interview process based on the candidate’s experience and qualifications. Adjustments outside of this range may be considered for candidates whose qualifications significantly differ from those outlined in the job description.\n   \n    \n   \n   Work Environment & Flexibility\n   \n   - 3-day hybrid in NYC\n   \n   - Unlimited PTO & 11 company holidays\n    \n   \n   Health & Wellness\n   \n   - Medical, dental, and vision benefits\n   \n   - Health Savings Account (HSA) & Flexible Spending Account (FSA)\n   \n   - Long- and short-term disability coverage\n   \n   - Annual employee wellness stipend\n    \n   \n   Family & Future Planning\n   \n   - 401(k) plan\n   \n   - Parental leave & family planning support benefits\n    \n   \n   Additional Perks\n   \n   - Company-issued laptop\n   \n   - Annual work-from-home stipend\n   \n   - Commuter benefits (if applicable)\n   \n   - A collaborative, mission-driven culture focused on improving patient care\n\n\n\nAt Allara https://www.allarahealth.com/, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7089ee4a-ac28-4a85-b260-30169eaf1482","title":"Telehealth Registered Dietitian | FT W2","department":"Clinical","team":"Registered Dietitian","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Florida","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T21:49:47.751+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Florida","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/7089ee4a-ac28-4a85-b260-30169eaf1482","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/7089ee4a-ac28-4a85-b260-30169eaf1482/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com\"><strong>Allara</strong></a> is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf\"><strong>health outcomes</strong></a>. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring  <strong>Registered Dietitians</strong> who want to focus on what matters most: delivering exceptional care to women who have historically been underserved. To learn more about our mission and clinical approach, visit <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://allarahealth.com\"><u>allarahealth.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Fully remote within the U.S.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your Impact</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze intake assessments, including medical history, dietary habits, laboratory results, and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct diet and lifestyle counseling and education sessions via video, including offering general movement, sleep, or stress management advice as needed and related to nutrition care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employ Allara’s provided nutrition training and educational materials to ensure consistent care while adapting to patient needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Incorporate motivational interviewing and behavior change techniques throughout the continuity of care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with APRNs and MDs involved in the medical management of your patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate and up-to-date patient records.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Responsibilities also include charting, addressing patient inquiries, and responding to administrative tasks and messages in a timely manner.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certification: </strong>Registered Dietitian with current certification from the Commission on Dietetic Registration <strong>(CDR)</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience: </strong>1-year experience treating patients with complex women’s health conditions (strongly desired).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical Independence: </strong>Proven ability to function as an autonomous provider with strong diagnostic judgment and critical thinking skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication:</strong> Exceptional written and verbal communication, with an emphasis on compassion and clarity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Webside Manner: </strong>A natural ability to build trust and connection with patients in a virtual setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evidence-Based Practice: </strong>A genuine commitment to delivering care rooted in current clinical research</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency: </strong>Comfortable working across multiple platforms including EMR systems, text expanders, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Telemedicine Experience: </strong>Prior telehealth experience is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>State License Requirements &amp; Hiring Considerations: </strong>An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered professional license in at least one U.S. state is required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>A note on state licensing:</strong> All active and pending licenses held at the time of application are collected and reviewed during our process. Hiring decisions reflect current state-level needs, which evolve over time. Applicants may not move forward immediately if there is no active need in their licensed states. We regularly revisit candidates as needs expand and when experience, licensure, and role requirements align.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Allara Offers</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual base salary: </strong>$65,000 + the ability to increase up to $105,000 through our incentive compensation program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health and Wellness:</strong> Medical, dental, and vision benefits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Future Planning:</strong> 401(k) plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off:</strong> Annual vacation, sick days, and holidays</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual CEU/WFH Stipend</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Continuing Education: </strong>Access to multiple free, live CEU sessions every month, plus a Women's Health Certificate of Training launching in 2027!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote:</strong> Work from anywhere in the U.S.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Scheduling:</strong> Set your schedule within full-time hour requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Malpractice Insurance:</strong> Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-Driven Work:</strong> Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborative Provider Network:</strong> Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inclusive Culture:</strong> Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com/\"><strong><u>Allara</u></strong></a>, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Allara https://www.allarahealth.com is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved health outcomes https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.\n\n\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe’re hiring  Registered Dietitians who want to focus on what matters most: delivering exceptional care to women who have historically been underserved. To learn more about our mission and clinical approach, visit allarahealth.com http://allarahealth.com.\n\n\n\nLocation: Fully remote within the U.S.\n\n\n\nYour Impact\n\n - Analyze intake assessments, including medical history, dietary habits, laboratory results, and more.\n\n - Conduct diet and lifestyle counseling and education sessions via video, including offering general movement, sleep, or stress management advice as needed and related to nutrition care.\n\n - Employ Allara’s provided nutrition training and educational materials to ensure consistent care while adapting to patient needs.\n\n - Incorporate motivational interviewing and behavior change techniques throughout the continuity of care.\n\n - Collaborate with APRNs and MDs involved in the medical management of your patients.\n\n - Maintain accurate and up-to-date patient records.\n\n - Responsibilities also include charting, addressing patient inquiries, and responding to administrative tasks and messages in a timely manner.\n\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n - Certification: Registered Dietitian with current certification from the Commission on Dietetic Registration (CDR).\n\n - Experience: 1-year experience treating patients with complex women’s health conditions (strongly desired).\n\n - Clinical Independence: Proven ability to function as an autonomous provider with strong diagnostic judgment and critical thinking skills\n\n - Communication: Exceptional written and verbal communication, with an emphasis on compassion and clarity\n\n - Webside Manner: A natural ability to build trust and connection with patients in a virtual setting\n\n - Evidence-Based Practice: A genuine commitment to delivering care rooted in current clinical research\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Comfortable working across multiple platforms including EMR systems, text expanders, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling tools\n\n - Telemedicine Experience: Prior telehealth experience is a plus\n\n - State License Requirements & Hiring Considerations: An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered professional license in at least one U.S. state is required.\n\n\n\nA note on state licensing: All active and pending licenses held at the time of application are collected and reviewed during our process. Hiring decisions reflect current state-level needs, which evolve over time. Applicants may not move forward immediately if there is no active need in their licensed states. We regularly revisit candidates as needs expand and when experience, licensure, and role requirements align.\n\n\n\nWhat Allara Offers\n\n - Annual base salary: $65,000 + the ability to increase up to $105,000 through our incentive compensation program\n\n - Health and Wellness: Medical, dental, and vision benefits\n\n - Future Planning: 401(k) plan\n\n - Time Off: Annual vacation, sick days, and holidays\n\n - Annual CEU/WFH Stipend\n\n - Continuing Education: Access to multiple free, live CEU sessions every month, plus a Women's Health Certificate of Training launching in 2027!\n\n - Fully Remote: Work from anywhere in the U.S.\n\n - Flexible Scheduling: Set your schedule within full-time hour requirements\n\n - Malpractice Insurance: Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you\n\n - Mission-Driven Work: Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated\n\n - Collaborative Provider Network: Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians\n\n - Inclusive Culture: Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging\n\n\n\nAt Allara https://www.allarahealth.com/, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d2be1d0e-b9ae-42d1-99ba-da6bad81d061","title":"Telehealth Registered Dietitian | FT W2","department":"Clinical","team":"Registered Dietitian","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Virginia","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T21:49:51.808+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Virginia","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/d2be1d0e-b9ae-42d1-99ba-da6bad81d061","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/d2be1d0e-b9ae-42d1-99ba-da6bad81d061/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com\"><strong>Allara</strong></a> is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf\"><strong>health outcomes</strong></a>. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring  <strong>Registered Dietitians</strong> who want to focus on what matters most: delivering exceptional care to women who have historically been underserved. To learn more about our mission and clinical approach, visit <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://allarahealth.com\"><u>allarahealth.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Fully remote within the U.S.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your Impact</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze intake assessments, including medical history, dietary habits, laboratory results, and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct diet and lifestyle counseling and education sessions via video, including offering general movement, sleep, or stress management advice as needed and related to nutrition care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employ Allara’s provided nutrition training and educational materials to ensure consistent care while adapting to patient needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Incorporate motivational interviewing and behavior change techniques throughout the continuity of care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with APRNs and MDs involved in the medical management of your patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate and up-to-date patient records.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Responsibilities also include charting, addressing patient inquiries, and responding to administrative tasks and messages in a timely manner.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certification: </strong>Registered Dietitian with current certification from the Commission on Dietetic Registration <strong>(CDR)</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience: </strong>1-year experience treating patients with complex women’s health conditions (strongly desired).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical Independence: </strong>Proven ability to function as an autonomous provider with strong diagnostic judgment and critical thinking skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication:</strong> Exceptional written and verbal communication, with an emphasis on compassion and clarity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Webside Manner: </strong>A natural ability to build trust and connection with patients in a virtual setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evidence-Based Practice: </strong>A genuine commitment to delivering care rooted in current clinical research</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency: </strong>Comfortable working across multiple platforms including EMR systems, text expanders, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Telemedicine Experience: </strong>Prior telehealth experience is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>State License Requirements &amp; Hiring Considerations: </strong>An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered professional license in at least one U.S. state is required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>A note on state licensing:</strong> All active and pending licenses held at the time of application are collected and reviewed during our process. Hiring decisions reflect current state-level needs, which evolve over time. Applicants may not move forward immediately if there is no active need in their licensed states. We regularly revisit candidates as needs expand and when experience, licensure, and role requirements align.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Allara Offers</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual base salary: </strong>$65,000 + the ability to increase up to $105,000 through our incentive compensation program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health and Wellness:</strong> Medical, dental, and vision benefits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Future Planning:</strong> 401(k) plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off:</strong> Annual vacation, sick days, and holidays</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual CEU/WFH Stipend</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Continuing Education: </strong>Access to multiple free, live CEU sessions every month, plus a Women's Health Certificate of Training launching in 2027!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote:</strong> Work from anywhere in the U.S.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Scheduling:</strong> Set your schedule within full-time hour requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Malpractice Insurance:</strong> Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-Driven Work:</strong> Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborative Provider Network:</strong> Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inclusive Culture:</strong> Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com/\"><strong><u>Allara</u></strong></a>, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Allara https://www.allarahealth.com is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved health outcomes https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.\n\n\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe’re hiring  Registered Dietitians who want to focus on what matters most: delivering exceptional care to women who have historically been underserved. To learn more about our mission and clinical approach, visit allarahealth.com http://allarahealth.com.\n\n\n\nLocation: Fully remote within the U.S.\n\n\n\nYour Impact\n\n - Analyze intake assessments, including medical history, dietary habits, laboratory results, and more.\n\n - Conduct diet and lifestyle counseling and education sessions via video, including offering general movement, sleep, or stress management advice as needed and related to nutrition care.\n\n - Employ Allara’s provided nutrition training and educational materials to ensure consistent care while adapting to patient needs.\n\n - Incorporate motivational interviewing and behavior change techniques throughout the continuity of care.\n\n - Collaborate with APRNs and MDs involved in the medical management of your patients.\n\n - Maintain accurate and up-to-date patient records.\n\n - Responsibilities also include charting, addressing patient inquiries, and responding to administrative tasks and messages in a timely manner.\n\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n - Certification: Registered Dietitian with current certification from the Commission on Dietetic Registration (CDR).\n\n - Experience: 1-year experience treating patients with complex women’s health conditions (strongly desired).\n\n - Clinical Independence: Proven ability to function as an autonomous provider with strong diagnostic judgment and critical thinking skills\n\n - Communication: Exceptional written and verbal communication, with an emphasis on compassion and clarity\n\n - Webside Manner: A natural ability to build trust and connection with patients in a virtual setting\n\n - Evidence-Based Practice: A genuine commitment to delivering care rooted in current clinical research\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Comfortable working across multiple platforms including EMR systems, text expanders, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling tools\n\n - Telemedicine Experience: Prior telehealth experience is a plus\n\n - State License Requirements & Hiring Considerations: An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered professional license in at least one U.S. state is required.\n\n\n\nA note on state licensing: All active and pending licenses held at the time of application are collected and reviewed during our process. Hiring decisions reflect current state-level needs, which evolve over time. Applicants may not move forward immediately if there is no active need in their licensed states. We regularly revisit candidates as needs expand and when experience, licensure, and role requirements align.\n\n\n\nWhat Allara Offers\n\n - Annual base salary: $65,000 + the ability to increase up to $105,000 through our incentive compensation program\n\n - Health and Wellness: Medical, dental, and vision benefits\n\n - Future Planning: 401(k) plan\n\n - Time Off: Annual vacation, sick days, and holidays\n\n - Annual CEU/WFH Stipend\n\n - Continuing Education: Access to multiple free, live CEU sessions every month, plus a Women's Health Certificate of Training launching in 2027!\n\n - Fully Remote: Work from anywhere in the U.S.\n\n - Flexible Scheduling: Set your schedule within full-time hour requirements\n\n - Malpractice Insurance: Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you\n\n - Mission-Driven Work: Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated\n\n - Collaborative Provider Network: Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians\n\n - Inclusive Culture: Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging\n\n\n\nAt Allara https://www.allarahealth.com/, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6beac031-e1bf-405d-8777-5a6b077f4d5d","title":"Telehealth Registered Dietitian | FT W2","department":"Clinical","team":"Registered Dietitian","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"North Carolina","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T21:49:53.647+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"North Carolina","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/6beac031-e1bf-405d-8777-5a6b077f4d5d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/6beac031-e1bf-405d-8777-5a6b077f4d5d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com\"><strong>Allara</strong></a> is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, 