nosed and undertreated\n\n - Collaborative Provider Network: Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians\n\n - Inclusive Culture: Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging\n\n\n\nAt Allara https://www.allarahealth.com/, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0ecc6909-cf61-477a-842a-5c6b234aeae0","title":"Telehealth Registered Dietitian | FT W2","department":"Clinical","team":"Registered Dietitian","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"District of Columbia (DC)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T21:49:49.668+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"DC","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/0ecc6909-cf61-477a-842a-5c6b234aeae0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/0ecc6909-cf61-477a-842a-5c6b234aeae0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com\"><strong>Allara</strong></a> is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf\"><strong>health outcomes</strong></a>. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring  <strong>Registered Dietitians</strong> who want to focus on what matters most: delivering exceptional care to women who have historically been underserved. To learn more about our mission and clinical approach, visit <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://allarahealth.com\"><u>allarahealth.com</u></a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Fully remote within the U.S.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your Impact</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze intake assessments, including medical history, dietary habits, laboratory results, and more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct diet and lifestyle counseling and education sessions via video, including offering general movement, sleep, or stress management advice as needed and related to nutrition care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employ Allara’s provided nutrition training and educational materials to ensure consistent care while adapting to patient needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Incorporate motivational interviewing and behavior change techniques throughout the continuity of care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with APRNs and MDs involved in the medical management of your patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate and up-to-date patient records.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Responsibilities also include charting, addressing patient inquiries, and responding to administrative tasks and messages in a timely manner.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certification: </strong>Registered Dietitian with current certification from the Commission on Dietetic Registration <strong>(CDR)</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience: </strong>1-year experience treating patients with complex women’s health conditions (strongly desired).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Clinical Independence: </strong>Proven ability to function as an autonomous provider with strong diagnostic judgment and critical thinking skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication:</strong> Exceptional written and verbal communication, with an emphasis on compassion and clarity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Webside Manner: </strong>A natural ability to build trust and connection with patients in a virtual setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evidence-Based Practice: </strong>A genuine commitment to delivering care rooted in current clinical research</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency: </strong>Comfortable working across multiple platforms including EMR systems, text expanders, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Telemedicine Experience: </strong>Prior telehealth experience is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>State License Requirements &amp; Hiring Considerations: </strong>An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered professional license in at least one U.S. state is required.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em><strong>A note on state licensing:</strong> All active and pending licenses held at the time of application are collected and reviewed during our process. Hiring decisions reflect current state-level needs, which evolve over time. Applicants may not move forward immediately if there is no active need in their licensed states. We regularly revisit candidates as needs expand and when experience, licensure, and role requirements align.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Allara Offers</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual base salary: </strong>$65,000 + the ability to increase up to $105,000 through our incentive compensation program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Health and Wellness:</strong> Medical, dental, and vision benefits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Future Planning:</strong> 401(k) plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Off:</strong> Annual vacation, sick days, and holidays</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual CEU/WFH Stipend</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Continuing Education: </strong>Access to multiple free, live CEU sessions every month, plus a Women's Health Certificate of Training launching in 2027!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote:</strong> Work from anywhere in the U.S.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Scheduling:</strong> Set your schedule within full-time hour requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Malpractice Insurance:</strong> Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-Driven Work:</strong> Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborative Provider Network:</strong> Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inclusive Culture:</strong> Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com/\"><strong><u>Allara</u></strong></a>, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Allara https://www.allarahealth.com is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved health outcomes https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.\n\n\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe’re hiring  Registered Dietitians who want to focus on what matters most: delivering exceptional care to women who have historically been underserved. To learn more about our mission and clinical approach, visit allarahealth.com http://allarahealth.com.\n\n\n\nLocation: Fully remote within the U.S.\n\n\n\nYour Impact\n\n - Analyze intake assessments, including medical history, dietary habits, laboratory results, and more.\n\n - Conduct diet and lifestyle counseling and education sessions via video, including offering general movement, sleep, or stress management advice as needed and related to nutrition care.\n\n - Employ Allara’s provided nutrition training and educational materials to ensure consistent care while adapting to patient needs.\n\n - Incorporate motivational interviewing and behavior change techniques throughout the continuity of care.\n\n - Collaborate with APRNs and MDs involved in the medical management of your patients.\n\n - Maintain accurate and up-to-date patient records.\n\n - Responsibilities also include charting, addressing patient inquiries, and responding to administrative tasks and messages in a timely manner.\n\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n - Certification: Registered Dietitian with current certification from the Commission on Dietetic Registration (CDR).\n\n - Experience: 1-year experience treating patients with complex women’s health conditions (strongly desired).\n\n - Clinical Independence: Proven ability to function as an autonomous provider with strong diagnostic judgment and critical thinking skills\n\n - Communication: Exceptional written and verbal communication, with an emphasis on compassion and clarity\n\n - Webside Manner: A natural ability to build trust and connection with patients in a virtual setting\n\n - Evidence-Based Practice: A genuine commitment to delivering care rooted in current clinical research\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Comfortable working across multiple platforms including EMR systems, text expanders, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling tools\n\n - Telemedicine Experience: Prior telehealth experience is a plus\n\n - State License Requirements & Hiring Considerations: An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered professional license in at least one U.S. state is required.\n\n\n\nA note on state licensing: All active and pending licenses held at the time of application are collected and reviewed during our process. Hiring decisions reflect current state-level needs, which evolve over time. Applicants may not move forward immediately if there is no active need in their licensed states. We regularly revisit candidates as needs expand and when experience, licensure, and role requirements align.\n\n\n\nWhat Allara Offers\n\n - Annual base salary: $65,000 + the ability to increase up to $105,000 through our incentive compensation program\n\n - Health and Wellness: Medical, dental, and vision benefits\n\n - Future Planning: 401(k) plan\n\n - Time Off: Annual vacation, sick days, and holidays\n\n - Annual CEU/WFH Stipend\n\n - Continuing Education: Access to multiple free, live CEU sessions every month, plus a Women's Health Certificate of Training launching in 2027!\n\n - Fully Remote: Work from anywhere in the U.S.\n\n - Flexible Scheduling: Set your schedule within full-time hour requirements\n\n - Malpractice Insurance: Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you\n\n - Mission-Driven Work: Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated\n\n - Collaborative Provider Network: Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians\n\n - Inclusive Culture: Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging\n\n\n\nAt Allara https://www.allarahealth.com/, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f2f2c80c-f901-4870-acca-33ba11f96395","title":"Remote Psychiatrist - Part-Time 1099","department":"Clinical","team":"Psychiatry - Physician","employmentType":"Contract","location":"New York","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-24T12:37:26.502+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/f2f2c80c-f901-4870-acca-33ba11f96395","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/f2f2c80c-f901-4870-acca-33ba11f96395/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com\"><strong>Allara</strong></a> is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf\"><strong>health outcomes</strong></a>. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're seeking a <strong>Consulting Psychiatrist </strong>to launch Allara's Psychiatry Service Line, as Allara Health expands its care model to include psychiatric services for women navigating the intersection of hormonal and mental health, and we're looking for a board-certified psychiatrist to support the launch right from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a consulting engagement supporting the clinical infrastructure for Allara's psychiatry service line. You'll work closely with our clinical and operations leadership to design the protocols, safeguards, and hiring standards that will define how we deliver psychiatric care to our patients. Once launched, you’ll treat your own panel of patients as well as provide supervision and case consultations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Fully remote within the U.S.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your Impact </strong><br /><br /><strong>Pre-Launch</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop clinical protocols for the treatment of mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD, including medication management and therapeutic modalities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design safety and escalation protocols for behavioral health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a hiring rubric and assessment framework for PMHNP candidates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in initial PMHNP interviews alongside our clinical team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Post-Launch</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate 50% of your time to treating patients experiencing mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supervise PMHNPs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide case consultations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support on ad-hoc escalations</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Board Certification: </strong>Active board certification in Psychiatry through the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN) or the American Osteopathic Board of Neurology and Psychiatry (AOBNP).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Licensure:</strong> An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered medical license in at least one of the following states: California, Florida, New York, or Texas. An IMLC license can be considered if willing to obtain an IMLC state mentioned above. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience: </strong>Minimum of 5 years of post-residency clinical experience as a practicing psychiatrist, with a focus on outpatient care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Women's Mental Health: </strong>Demonstrated experience treating conditions at the intersection of hormonal and mental health, including depression, anxiety, and PMDD.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Supervision:</strong> Experience supervising or collaborating with psychiatric nurse practitioners (PMHNPs) or other advanced practice providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems Building: </strong>Ability to translate clinical rigor into scalable protocols, safety standards, and hiring frameworks in a fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication &amp; Webside Manner: </strong>Exceptional written and verbal communication, with a strong ability to connect with patients virtually and deliver empathetic, evidence-based care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency:</strong> Comfortable navigating multiple screens and tools such as EMR, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling platforms.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in a telehealth or high-growth care delivery environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing behavioral health safety and escalation protocols.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Commitment</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pre-Launch: </strong>5 hours/wk from September-26 to February-27</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Post- Launch:</strong> 10 hours/wk from March-27 onwards</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Allara Offers</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1099 Contract: </strong>The flexibility and autonomy of an independent contractor arrangement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation:</strong> $200/hr.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1099 Longevity Recognition Bonus</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote: </strong>Work from anywhere in the U.S.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Scheduling:</strong> Set hours that fit your life, not the other way around</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Malpractice Insurance: </strong>Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-Driven Work: </strong>Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborative Provider Network: </strong>Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inclusive Culture:</strong> Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com/\"><strong><u>Allara</u></strong></a>, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Allara https://www.allarahealth.com is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved health outcomes https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.\n\n\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe're seeking a Consulting Psychiatrist to launch Allara's Psychiatry Service Line, as Allara Health expands its care model to include psychiatric services for women navigating the intersection of hormonal and mental health, and we're looking for a board-certified psychiatrist to support the launch right from the ground up.\n\n\n\nThis is a consulting engagement supporting the clinical infrastructure for Allara's psychiatry service line. You'll work closely with our clinical and operations leadership to design the protocols, safeguards, and hiring standards that will define how we deliver psychiatric care to our patients. Once launched, you’ll treat your own panel of patients as well as provide supervision and case consultations.\n\n\n\nLocation: Fully remote within the U.S.\n\n\n\nYour Impact \n\nPre-Launch\n\n - Develop clinical protocols for the treatment of mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD, including medication management and therapeutic modalities\n\n - Design safety and escalation protocols for behavioral health\n\n - Build a hiring rubric and assessment framework for PMHNP candidates\n\n - Participate in initial PMHNP interviews alongside our clinical team\n\n\n\nPost-Launch\n\n - Allocate 50% of your time to treating patients experiencing mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD\n\n - Supervise PMHNPs\n\n - Provide case consultations\n\n - Support on ad-hoc escalations\n\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n - Board Certification: Active board certification in Psychiatry through the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN) or the American Osteopathic Board of Neurology and Psychiatry (AOBNP).\n\n - Licensure: An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered medical license in at least one of the following states: California, Florida, New York, or Texas. An IMLC license can be considered if willing to obtain an IMLC state mentioned above. \n\n - Experience: Minimum of 5 years of post-residency clinical experience as a practicing psychiatrist, with a focus on outpatient care.\n\n - Women's Mental Health: Demonstrated experience treating conditions at the intersection of hormonal and mental health, including depression, anxiety, and PMDD.\n\n - Supervision: Experience supervising or collaborating with psychiatric nurse practitioners (PMHNPs) or other advanced practice providers.\n\n - Systems Building: Ability to translate clinical rigor into scalable protocols, safety standards, and hiring frameworks in a fast-moving environment.\n\n - Communication & Webside Manner: Exceptional written and verbal communication, with a strong ability to connect with patients virtually and deliver empathetic, evidence-based care.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Comfortable navigating multiple screens and tools such as EMR, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling platforms.\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Prior experience in a telehealth or high-growth care delivery environment.\n\n - Experience designing behavioral health safety and escalation protocols.\n\n\n\nTime Commitment\n\n - Pre-Launch: 5 hours/wk from September-26 to February-27\n\n - Post- Launch: 10 hours/wk from March-27 onwards\n\n\n\nWhat Allara Offers\n\n - 1099 Contract: The flexibility and autonomy of an independent contractor arrangement\n\n - Compensation: $200/hr.\n\n - 1099 Longevity Recognition Bonus\n\n - Fully Remote: Work from anywhere in the U.S.\n\n - Flexible Scheduling: Set hours that fit your life, not the other way around\n\n - Malpractice Insurance: Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you\n\n - Mission-Driven Work: Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated\n\n - Collaborative Provider Network: Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians\n\n - Inclusive Culture: Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging\n\n\n\nAt Allara https://www.allarahealth.com/, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c0d045d1-2065-4816-bc31-7aa741197a48","title":"Remote Psychiatrist - Part-Time 1099","department":"Clinical","team":"Psychiatry - Physician","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Texas","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-24T12:37:05.927+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Texas","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/c0d045d1-2065-4816-bc31-7aa741197a48","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/c0d045d1-2065-4816-bc31-7aa741197a48/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com\"><strong>Allara</strong></a> is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf\"><strong>health outcomes</strong></a>. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're seeking a <strong>Consulting Psychiatrist </strong>to launch Allara's Psychiatry Service Line, as Allara Health expands its care model to include psychiatric services for women navigating the intersection of hormonal and mental health, and we're looking for a board-certified psychiatrist to support the launch right from the ground up.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a consulting engagement supporting the clinical infrastructure for Allara's psychiatry service line. You'll work closely with our clinical and operations leadership to design the protocols, safeguards, and hiring standards that will define how we deliver psychiatric care to our patients. Once launched, you’ll treat your own panel of patients as well as provide supervision and case consultations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Fully remote within the U.S.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Your Impact </strong><br /><br /><strong>Pre-Launch</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop clinical protocols for the treatment of mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD, including medication management and therapeutic modalities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design safety and escalation protocols for behavioral health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a hiring rubric and assessment framework for PMHNP candidates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in initial PMHNP interviews alongside our clinical team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Post-Launch</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allocate 50% of your time to treating patients experiencing mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supervise PMHNPs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide case consultations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support on ad-hoc escalations</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Board Certification: </strong>Active board certification in Psychiatry through the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN) or the American Osteopathic Board of Neurology and Psychiatry (AOBNP).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Licensure:</strong> An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered medical license in at least one of the following states: California, Florida, New York, or Texas. An IMLC license can be considered if willing to obtain an IMLC state mentioned above. </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience: </strong>Minimum of 5 years of post-residency clinical experience as a practicing psychiatrist, with a focus on outpatient care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Women's Mental Health: </strong>Demonstrated experience treating conditions at the intersection of hormonal and mental health, including depression, anxiety, and PMDD.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Supervision:</strong> Experience supervising or collaborating with psychiatric nurse practitioners (PMHNPs) or other advanced practice providers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Systems Building: </strong>Ability to translate clinical rigor into scalable protocols, safety standards, and hiring frameworks in a fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication &amp; Webside Manner: </strong>Exceptional written and verbal communication, with a strong ability to connect with patients virtually and deliver empathetic, evidence-based care.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Proficiency:</strong> Comfortable navigating multiple screens and tools such as EMR, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling platforms.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in a telehealth or high-growth care delivery environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing behavioral health safety and escalation protocols.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time Commitment</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pre-Launch: </strong>5 hours/wk from September-26 to February-27</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Post- Launch:</strong> 10 hours/wk from March-27 onwards</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Allara Offers</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1099 Contract: </strong>The flexibility and autonomy of an independent contractor arrangement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation:</strong> $200/hr.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1099 Longevity Recognition Bonus</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Remote: </strong>Work from anywhere in the U.S.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Scheduling:</strong> Set hours that fit your life, not the other way around</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Malpractice Insurance: </strong>Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-Driven Work: </strong>Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Collaborative Provider Network: </strong>Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Inclusive Culture:</strong> Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com/\"><strong><u>Allara</u></strong></a>, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Allara https://www.allarahealth.com is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved health outcomes https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.\n\n\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe're seeking a Consulting Psychiatrist to launch Allara's Psychiatry Service Line, as Allara Health expands its care model to include psychiatric services for women navigating the intersection of hormonal and mental health, and we're looking for a board-certified psychiatrist to support the launch right from the ground up.\n\n\n\nThis is a consulting engagement supporting the clinical infrastructure for Allara's psychiatry service line. You'll work closely with our clinical and operations leadership to design the protocols, safeguards, and hiring standards that will define how we deliver psychiatric care to our patients. Once launched, you’ll treat your own panel of patients as well as provide supervision and case consultations.\n\n\n\nLocation: Fully remote within the U.S.\n\n\n\nYour Impact \n\nPre-Launch\n\n - Develop clinical protocols for the treatment of mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD, including medication management and therapeutic modalities\n\n - Design safety and escalation protocols for behavioral health\n\n - Build a hiring rubric and assessment framework for PMHNP candidates\n\n - Participate in initial PMHNP interviews alongside our clinical team\n\n\n\nPost-Launch\n\n - Allocate 50% of your time to treating patients experiencing mild to moderate depression, anxiety, and PMDD\n\n - Supervise PMHNPs\n\n - Provide case consultations\n\n - Support on ad-hoc escalations\n\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n - Board Certification: Active board certification in Psychiatry through the American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN) or the American Osteopathic Board of Neurology and Psychiatry (AOBNP).\n\n - Licensure: An active, unrestricted, and unencumbered medical license in at least one of the following states: California, Florida, New York, or Texas. An IMLC license can be considered if willing to obtain an IMLC state mentioned above. \n\n - Experience: Minimum of 5 years of post-residency clinical experience as a practicing psychiatrist, with a focus on outpatient care.\n\n - Women's Mental Health: Demonstrated experience treating conditions at the intersection of hormonal and mental health, including depression, anxiety, and PMDD.\n\n - Supervision: Experience supervising or collaborating with psychiatric nurse practitioners (PMHNPs) or other advanced practice providers.\n\n - Systems Building: Ability to translate clinical rigor into scalable protocols, safety standards, and hiring frameworks in a fast-moving environment.\n\n - Communication & Webside Manner: Exceptional written and verbal communication, with a strong ability to connect with patients virtually and deliver empathetic, evidence-based care.\n\n - Technical Proficiency: Comfortable navigating multiple screens and tools such as EMR, Gmail, Google Calendar, Zoom, and scheduling platforms.\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Prior experience in a telehealth or high-growth care delivery environment.\n\n - Experience designing behavioral health safety and escalation protocols.\n\n\n\nTime Commitment\n\n - Pre-Launch: 5 hours/wk from September-26 to February-27\n\n - Post- Launch: 10 hours/wk from March-27 onwards\n\n\n\nWhat Allara Offers\n\n - 1099 Contract: The flexibility and autonomy of an independent contractor arrangement\n\n - Compensation: $200/hr.\n\n - 1099 Longevity Recognition Bonus\n\n - Fully Remote: Work from anywhere in the U.S.\n\n - Flexible Scheduling: Set hours that fit your life, not the other way around\n\n - Malpractice Insurance: Comprehensive coverage provided at no cost to you\n\n - Mission-Driven Work: Help transform the standard of care for women living with conditions that have historically been underdiagnosed and undertreated\n\n - Collaborative Provider Network: Connect with and learn from a community of skilled, like-minded Allara clinicians\n\n - Inclusive Culture: Join a supportive, diverse team that values innovation, equity, and belonging\n\n\n\nAt Allara https://www.allarahealth.com/, we believe in celebrating everything that makes us human and are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We embrace diversity and are committed to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. We believe that the more inclusive we are, the better we can serve our members. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against candidates or patients based on race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"08d094ec-7acf-49aa-818a-3a7b4472d0bc","title":"Remote Psychiatrist - Part-Time 1099","department":"Clinical","team":"Psychiatry - Physician","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Florida","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-24T12:36:28.893+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Florida","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/08d094ec-7acf-49aa-818a-3a7b4472d0bc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/allarahealth/08d094ec-7acf-49aa-818a-3a7b4472d0bc/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.allarahealth.com\"><strong>Allara</strong></a> is a comprehensive women’s health provider that specializes in expert, longitudinal care that supports women through every life stage. Trusted by over 60,000 women nationwide, Allara makes expert healthcare accessible by connecting patients with multidisciplinary care teams that have a deep understanding of hormonal, metabolic, and reproductive care. Allara provides ongoing support for hormonal conditions like PCOS, chronic conditions like insulin resistance, and life stages like perimenopause, helping patients see improved <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/637f55cdd2e0aa051d497c52/68e6aa0f8fcce5c60e922219_Outcomes%20Impact%20Report%202025%20Web%20Display.pdf\"><strong>health outcomes</strong></a>. As one of the fastest-growing women’s health platforms in the U.S., Allara is bridging long-overlooked gaps in healthcare for women.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style=\"min-heig